<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/NvdVersionStatus> skos:inScheme "https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/nvd_cve"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:definition_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/NvdVersionStatus"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:description "Whether a version of a product has the vulnerability." ;
	linkml:permissible_values <https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/affected> , <https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/unaffected> , <https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/unknown> .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/NvdVulnStatus> skos:inScheme "https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/nvd_cve"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:note "NVD's schema says only that vulnStatus is a string. This list comes from the data: the seven values of the 33,378 records read on 2026-11-03, which are the modified feed, the records the API marks as known exploited, and eight pages of its results spread across all its years. NVD's page that defines them refuses a plain client, so each description says only what the value's name and the data show. A new value fails validation, and the feed test reports it." ;
	linkml:definition_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/NvdVulnStatus"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:description "Where a vulnerability stands in NVD's own analysis." ;
	linkml:permissible_values <https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/Analyzed> , <https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/Awaiting%20Analysis> , <https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/Deferred> , <https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/Modified> , <https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/Received> , <https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/Rejected> , <https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/Undergoing%20Analysis> .
