<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/OFFICIAL_FIX> linkml:description "The vendor offers a complete fix." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/OR> linkml:description "At least one part must hold." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/PARTIAL> linkml:description "Some is lost, and the attacker cannot choose all of it." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/PASSIVE> linkml:description "Someone has to act only in the ordinary course of their work." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/PHYSICAL> linkml:description "Only by touching the hardware." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/PRESENT> linkml:description "People could be seriously hurt." , "The attack works only when the target is in a certain state." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/PROOF_OF_CONCEPT> linkml:description "A demonstration exists that needs skilled work to use." , "A demonstration is public, with no reported attack." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/Patch> linkml:description "The page holds or points to a fix." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/Permissions%20Required> linkml:description "Reading the page takes an account or some other access." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/Press/Media%20Coverage> linkml:description "A report in the press or other media." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/Primary> linkml:description "NVD's first source for the record." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/Product> linkml:description "A page about the affected product." , "A page about the product." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/Project> linkml:description "A page about the project behind the product." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/REASONABLE> linkml:description "Solid details exist, without full confirmation of the cause." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/RED> linkml:description "The supplier says the flaw is at the highest urgency." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/REQUIRED> linkml:description "Someone other than the attacker has to do something." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/Received> linkml:description "The record has just reached NVD." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/Recovery> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	linkml:annotations _:c14n274 ;
	linkml:description "How the affected system comes back after an attack." ;
	linkml:ifabsent "CvssV4Recovery(NOT_DEFINED)" ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/CvssV4Recovery> .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/Rejected> linkml:description "The CVE identifier has been rejected." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/Related> linkml:description "A page on a related matter." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/Release%20Notes> linkml:description "The notes of a product release." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/SAFETY> linkml:description "The loss could injure people." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/SINGLE> linkml:description "One login." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/Safety> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	linkml:annotations _:c14n74 ;
	linkml:description "Whether an attack could put people's safety at risk." ;
	linkml:ifabsent "CvssV4Safety(NOT_DEFINED)" ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/CvssV4Safety> .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/Secondary> linkml:description "Any other source." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/TEMPORARY_FIX> linkml:description "The vendor offers a stopgap for now." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/Technical%20Description> linkml:description "A technical account of the vulnerability." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/Third%20Party%20Advisory> linkml:description "An advisory from someone other than the vendor." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/Tool%20Signature> linkml:description "A signature that a detection tool can use." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/UNAVAILABLE> linkml:description "No fix exists, or it cannot be applied." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/UNCHANGED> linkml:description "The harm stays within the same security authority." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/UNCONFIRMED> linkml:description "A single report or conflicting reports that nobody has checked." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/UNCORROBORATED> linkml:description "Several unofficial sources agree, with some doubt remaining." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/UNKNOWN> linkml:description "Reports say something is wrong, but the cause is not clear." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/UNPROVEN> linkml:description "No attack code is known, or the attack is only theory." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/UNREPORTED> linkml:description "No demonstration or attack has been reported." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/URL%20Repurposed> linkml:description "The address now leads to something else." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/US%20Government%20Resource> linkml:description "A page from a body of the United States government." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/USER> linkml:description "Someone has to step in and restore it." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/Undergoing%20Analysis> linkml:description "NVD is analysing the record now." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/VDB%20Entry> linkml:description "An entry in a vulnerability database." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/Vendor%20Advisory> linkml:description "An advisory from the product's vendor." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/Vendor> linkml:description "A page about the vendor." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/Version> linkml:description "A page about this version." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/WORKAROUND> linkml:description "Others offer a way round the flaw that is not from the vendor." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/YES> linkml:description "Every step can be automated." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/acInsufInfo> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	linkml:description "Whether NVD lacked the information to rate the access complexity." ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/boolean> .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/accessComplexity> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	skos:closeMatch "sepses_cvss:accessComplexity"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:annotations _:c14n261 ;
	linkml:description "How hard the flaw is to use once the attacker can reach it." ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/CvssV2AccessComplexity> .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/accessVector> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	skos:closeMatch "sepses_cvss:accessVector"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:annotations _:c14n63 ;
	linkml:description "How far away an attacker can be when using the flaw, in CVSS 2.0's terms." ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/CvssV2AccessVector> .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/action> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	linkml:description "How the data changed, such as Added." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/affected> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	skos:closeMatch "cve:affected"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:description "The affected products, by the source that names them." , "This version has the vulnerability." ;
	linkml:inlined true ;
	linkml:inlined_as_list true ;
	linkml:multivalued true ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/NvdAffected> .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/affectedData> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	linkml:description "The products." ;
	linkml:inlined true ;
	linkml:inlined_as_list true ;
	linkml:minimum_cardinality 1 ;
	linkml:multivalued true ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/NvdAffectedProduct> ;
	linkml:required true .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/at> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	skos:inScheme "https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/nvd_cve"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:mappingRelation "https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/at"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:definition_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/at"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:description "The version at which the status changes." ;
	linkml:domain_of <https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/NvdVersionChange> ;
	linkml:owner <https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/NvdVersionChange> ;
	linkml:pattern "^[\\s\\S]{1,1024}$" ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/string> ;
	linkml:required true ;
	linkml:slot_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/at"^^xsd:anyURI .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/attackComplexity> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	skos:closeMatch "http://w3id.org/sepses/vocab/ref/cvss#attackComplexity"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:inScheme "https://w3id.org/lmodel/cve/cve_cvss"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:annotations _:c14n37 ;
	linkml:definition_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/cve/attackComplexity"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:description "How much is outside the attacker's control when using the flaw." ;
	linkml:domain_of <https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/CvssV30> , <https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/CvssV31> , <https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/CvssV40> ;
	linkml:owner <https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/CvssV40> ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/string> ;
	linkml:slot_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/cve/attackComplexity"^^xsd:anyURI .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/attackRequirements> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	linkml:annotations _:c14n284 ;
	linkml:description "Whether the attack needs conditions in the target that the attacker does not control." ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/CvssV4AttackRequirements> .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/attackVector> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	skos:closeMatch "http://w3id.org/sepses/vocab/ref/cvss#attackVector"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:inScheme "https://w3id.org/lmodel/cve/cve_cvss"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:annotations _:c14n46 ;
	linkml:definition_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/cve/attackVector"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:description "How far away an attacker can be when using the flaw." ;
	linkml:domain_of <https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/CvssV30> , <https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/CvssV31> , <https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/CvssV40> ;
	linkml:owner <https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/CvssV40> ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/string> ;
	linkml:slot_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/cve/attackVector"^^xsd:anyURI .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/nist-nvd/authentication> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	skos:closeMatch "sepses_cvss:authentication"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:annotations _:c14n6 ;
